  return (
    <UserRoleContext.Provider value={{ userRole, setUserRole }}>
      {children}
    </UserRoleContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

### Step 2: Protect Routes Based on User Roles

Next, create a custom route component that checks the user role before allowing access to the route.

```jsx
import React from 'react';
