### Step 1: Use Memoization

Memoization can help prevent unnecessary re-renders by ensuring that components only re-render when their props change. You can use `React.memo` to wrap your functional components.

### Step 2: Optimize Rendering

Ensure that you are not unnecessarily re-rendering large lists of items. You can use `React.lazy` and `Suspense` to load components lazily, which can help improve initial load times and reduce the number of components rendered at once.

### Step 3: Use Concurrent Mode

